###############################################################################
# REST Client Examples for Minimal App API (Student Notes)
###############################################################################
# Purpose:
# - Test API endpoints directly from VS Code using the REST Client extension
# - No need for Postman or curl commands
# - Great for learning HTTP methods and API design
#
# How to use:
# 1. Install "REST Client" extension by Humao (included in devcontainer)
# 2. Click "Send Request" above any ### line
# 3. Response appears in a new tab
#
# Teaching points:
# - HTTP methods: GET (read), POST (create), PUT (update), DELETE (delete)
# - Request headers: Content-Type tells server what format we're sending
# - Request body: JSON data for POST/PUT operations
# - Response status codes: 200 OK, 201 Created, 204 No Content, 404 Not Found
# - RESTful URL patterns: /api/resources and /api/resources/:id
###############################################################################

# Define base URL as a variable (change if your backend runs on different port)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@contentType = application/json

###############################################################################
# Health Check
###############################################################################

### Health Check - Backend status
# Expected: 200 OK with { "status": "ok", "database": "connected", "timestamp": "..." }
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

###############################################################################
# Categories
###############################################################################

### Get all categories
# Expected: 200 OK with array of category objects
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/categories

###############################################################################
# Products - List and Filter
###############################################################################

### Get all products (first page)
# Expected: 200 OK with { "data": [...], "meta": { "total": 10, "page": 1, ... } }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products

### Get products - page 2
# Teaching note: Pagination with query parameters
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?page=2&per_page=5

### Get products filtered by category
# Teaching note: Replace category_id=1 with actual category ID from categories endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?category_id=1

### Get products - multiple filters
# Teaching note: Combining pagination and filtering
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?page=1&per_page=3&category_id=2

###############################################################################
# Products - Single Product
###############################################################################

### Get product by ID
# Teaching note: Replace :id with actual product ID (e.g., 1, 2, 3)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1

### Get product by ID - Not Found test
# Expected: 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/999999

### Get product by ID - Invalid ID test
# Expected: 400 Bad Request or 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/invalid

###############################################################################
# Products - Create
###############################################################################

### Create new product - Full data
# Expected: 201 Created with new product object (includes auto-generated id, created_at)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Test Product from REST Client",
  "price": 29.99,
  "description": "Created via VS Code REST Client for testing",
  "category_id": 1,
  "image_url": "https://placehold.co/600x400?text=Test+Product"
}

### Create new product - Minimal data (no category, no image)
# Teaching note: category_id and image_url are optional
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Minimal Product",
  "price": 9.99,
  "description": "Just name, price, and description"
}

### Create new product - Validation error test (missing required field)
# Expected: 400 Bad Request with validation errors
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Incomplete Product"
}

### Create new product - Validation error test (invalid price)
# Expected: 400 Bad Request (price must be positive)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Invalid Price Product",
  "price": -10.00,
  "description": "Price is negative"
}

###############################################################################
# Products - Update
###############################################################################

### Update product - Full update
# Teaching note: PUT replaces entire resource. Include all fields.
# Replace :id with actual product ID you want to update
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Updated Product Name",
  "price": 39.99,
  "description": "This product was updated via REST Client",
  "category_id": 2,
  "image_url": "https://placehold.co/600x400?text=Updated"
}

### Update product - Partial update (change only price)
# Note: This API uses PUT (full replacement). PATCH would be for partial updates.
# You still need to send all required fields with PUT.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/2
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Existing Product Name",
  "price": 99.99,
  "description": "Only the price changed"
}

### Update product - Not Found test
# Expected: 404 Not Found
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/999999
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Non-existent Product",
  "price": 19.99,
  "description": "This ID doesn't exist"
}

###############################################################################
# Products - Delete
###############################################################################

### Delete product by ID
# Expected: 204 No Content (success, no response body)
# Warning: This actually deletes the product! Use a test ID you don't need.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/100

### Delete product - Not Found test
# Expected: 404 Not Found
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/999999

###############################################################################
# Error Handling Tests
###############################################################################

### Test 404 - Invalid endpoint
# Expected: 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/invalid-endpoint

### Test Method Not Allowed (if implemented)
# Expected: 405 Method Not Allowed or 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/categories
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "New Category"
}

###############################################################################
# Performance and Load Testing
###############################################################################

### Quick performance test - Sequential requests
# Teaching note: Click "Send Request" multiple times quickly to test performance
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products

###############################################################################
# Extension Points for Students
###############################################################################

# EXTENSION_POINT: api.auth | Add authentication endpoints | intermediate
# Examples:
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
# GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/profile
# Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>

# EXTENSION_POINT: api.search | Add full-text search | beginner
# Example:
# GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/search?q=laptop

# EXTENSION_POINT: api.reviews | Add product reviews | intermediate
# Examples:
# GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1/reviews
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1/reviews
# DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/:id

###############################################################################
# Tips for Students
###############################################################################
# 1. Variables: Define @baseUrl at top, use {{baseUrl}} throughout
# 2. Save response: Click "Save Response" to save JSON for analysis
# 3. Copy as curl: Right-click request → "Copy Request As cURL"
# 4. Environment variables: Create .env file for different environments
# 5. Chaining requests: Use response from one request in another (advanced)
# 6. Timing: Check response time in the response tab
# 7. Headers: View all response headers in the response tab
#
# Learn more: https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=humao.rest-client
###############################################################################
